[{"id":"VRCE-5-40-1","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":1,"english":"Then on account of the cries of birds and the sounds of breaking trees, all the denizons of Lankā were seized with trepidation in consequence of fright.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.785,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040001","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b0d0e34b975a805f2c527cc98b44fc70269ab6c567c433343e652d7d9367fef8","compact":"466a1bb3155d95ddf04dd174f01107f07cd93d4804beda53955a7a5801cb92f5","nasal":"3e6b194b33acb939041b52b7c48b96f2d8309cd201925ec5befba1b970cdc04a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-2","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":2,"english":"And agitated with fear, birds and beasts hurried (on all sides); and omens boding evil to the, Raksasas, began to appear (everywhere).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.706,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040002","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"951aa518bf7b4b45319c557d08a3c989770939a47485762b270c71ab792336e5","compact":"54ed82d7cf456a34d8639d977d12742637416c9a319700fbdebfd966f2379228","nasal":"54ed82d7cf456a34d8639d977d12742637416c9a319700fbdebfd966f2379228"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-3","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":3,"english":"And grim-visaged Rākṣasīs, awaking from their sleep, saw that wood devastated, and that heroic mighty monkey.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040003","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f8d9620be1d5ff56a74911d8351b2e42c239a767fe18253383f608c44541b8ef","compact":"7a953d7330bfb6f9ac9ca39a8b3bcc25a16bf4e876c616251185c635f2ce876d","nasal":"7a953d7330bfb6f9ac9ca39a8b3bcc25a16bf4e876c616251185c635f2ce876d"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-4","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":4,"english":"And observing them, that mighty-armed and powerful monkey endowed with immense strength, magnified his dimension, capable of striking terror into the Rākşasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.729,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040004","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7bfaaaff86776c034ee59a7c01d3759c14f351df2adc546ae5b8b0b20330acd6","compact":"7e6bbab2438c9e084d17f292e2c32d489c38eddc154b8085af9525ebbd136061","nasal":"7e6bbab2438c9e084d17f292e2c32d489c38eddc154b8085af9525ebbd136061"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-5","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":5,"english":"Beholding that exceedingly strong monkey resembling a mountain, the Räkşasīs asked Janaka's daughter, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.908,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040005","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6d593742a31b88cab953e34a5337aecb87df4a8ea79d092dc614a3bb3b43b33d","compact":"f648a405113a8e9134204ca72b5670c1c10854c4d57757b6cbcfffa1a69d0be9","nasal":"f648a405113a8e9134204ca72b5670c1c10854c4d57757b6cbcfffa1a69d0be9"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-6","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":6,"english":"Who is this? And whence, and wherefore has he come here? And why did he carry on converse with you? Tell us this, you of expansive eyes. O lucky one, entertain no fear. And, O you having eyes with dark outer corners, what is the talk that this one has held with you?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040006","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"15adc530098f572116fde9563573b6c20dc6ba4a86ddf5a8e5791131ff42b890","compact":"fc9e290679822578968e39c18e873a96382a5513884cfaa49f043d3a7239a9c8","nasal":"fc9e290679822578968e39c18e873a96382a5513884cfaa49f043d3a7239a9c8"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":7,"english":"Who is this? And whence, and wherefore has he come here? And why did he carry on converse with you? Tell us this, you of expansive eyes. O lucky one, entertain no fear. And, O you having eyes with dark outer corners, what is the talk that this one has held with you?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0407bdcbbe7ccf682da6838f0445d8716f71eae7c6561fe950deb4d0e0c416a1","compact":"b7a0b5a9dedea8cc3a8d287515c2955b65a7a9c69025d3f87c84d4cdd04eaeaf","nasal":"edd2b8b5e2e29f2c3f792f915006544c8145314a4d88a2c26d4c4d38dec399ac"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":8,"english":"Thereat, the chaste Sītā, having all her parts perfect, answered, “What is my power to read Rākṣasas capable of wearing forms at will? ”","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2ae6e526ffe84b91dc11de76e2ddbe99c0f34c124fa5d62668d1eb099fdff202","compact":"a76c456e532e2ad014408098fe6cbfe5294406def97c4fc0696bf2f4472910dc","nasal":"6a318a0b4a3136672419855f269394b061c7df91947358384d8ef13f7f2b721e"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":9,"english":"You know who he is and what he does. Serpents, without doubt, know the way of serpents.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040009","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7ddc09cdd50c73b7ff79d81fea8f3f5f58e0da802773d4b6e56e26d8f6780293","compact":"af1db545403b13e9e6708794fa38afa902499fb789931222cd0de0641bf193b2","nasal":"af1db545403b13e9e6708794fa38afa902499fb789931222cd0de0641bf193b2"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-10","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":10,"english":"And, furthermore, I am very much frightened, nor know I who that one is. I take him to be a Rākşasa, who has come here through his capacity to put on any shape.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.517,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040010","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"06d021a6e6c345aa8c104f8d87c25cfed374b6cad79e1425c5b2dcaf98eee34d","compact":"2729faacbfd9bd2d61f013b81507fb1cfcfef48d7883970a31a9405c371aa5cf","nasal":"2729faacbfd9bd2d61f013b81507fb1cfcfef48d7883970a31a9405c371aa5cf"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-11","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":11,"english":"Hearing Vaidehi's words, the Raksasis swiftly took to their heels. Some remained, and some departed to inform Rāvana of the matter.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.812,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040011","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8d09a342b0ee8d144f7d36d1995cca2363029e4186ef8faf5a253a070980a42c","compact":"9a9f8b755ed161072b32036a3c2b737bc4b39b48f30cfef5303f30be859f260f","nasal":"9a9f8b755ed161072b32036a3c2b737bc4b39b48f30cfef5303f30be859f260f"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-12","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":12,"english":"And before Rāvana, the Rākṣasīs of deformed visage informed him of the hideous and dreadful monkey.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.69,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040012","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ad372750e9faa0d9b019b3ae4408c32458ab74dd208ce40c4109f5c4aaf02658","compact":"c509f4b90b0d486e5a036cec8a801fb17153a50bd5682a7331a3ed56bbd253e2","nasal":"c509f4b90b0d486e5a036cec8a801fb17153a50bd5682a7331a3ed56bbd253e2"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-13","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":13,"english":"O king, in the heart of the aśoka wood there is a monkey of a terrific body, who, possessed of immeasurable might, stay, after having carried on a conversation with Jānakī.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040013","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dcacb8c2a70a1d355708912c1e99166d9b7736f240577c10a7a4a7e1d5ff37c7","compact":"cfeb16f699590d9a184cbec549bab1cf55ac9c3869528f302dc6d9fc0b1b6a0b","nasal":"cfeb16f699590d9a184cbec549bab1cf55ac9c3869528f302dc6d9fc0b1b6a0b"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-14","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":14,"english":"Nor, albeit questioned by us many a time and oft, dose Janaka's daughter, Sītā, having the eyes of a deer, intend to tell us who the monkey is.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.709,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040014","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d4822a5dc1d24045e41c47ccd21586c821ff781e0f3af07e7a76d75021866501","compact":"c6b767746352cdff6f746fce188f1a16875d6b87f08123690b4932a1d1fe50d1","nasal":"c6b767746352cdff6f746fce188f1a16875d6b87f08123690b4932a1d1fe50d1"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-15","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":15,"english":"He may be the emissary of Vāsava, or of Vaiśravaņa; or he may have been sent by Rāma himself from eagerness to get at the whereabouts of Sita.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.77,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040015","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"83426bbd317d02932dfaa381db7b2d74cb511300756a706a60bb3b07da61decb","compact":"f51939e3e281b9a76849c250e988389635fac87c3b933d2c90ec9a7dbaa61215","nasal":"dd964d1c4ceff4832841460588a341626a356955ac166cd3af5a33f23e74353b"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-16","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":16,"english":"And he it is that, wearing a wonderful form, has destroyed your charming arbour of the interior, filled with beasts of various kinds-And quarter there is none which has not been destroyer by him; and only that place where the exalted Jänakī is, remain uninjured by him.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040016","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0358eb5c4423a20a8ef03d44e3183c14398529012c9ad587d9a4c21814a7ca1c","compact":"fcd2ac91305d6afb9ac17b2794ba3c028e8fbd1dabf84517f933630c3e63dc58","nasal":"fcd2ac91305d6afb9ac17b2794ba3c028e8fbd1dabf84517f933630c3e63dc58"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-17","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":17,"english":"And he it is that, wearing a wonderful form, has destroyed your charming arbour of the interior, filled with beasts of various kinds-And quarter there is none which has not been destroyer by him; and only that place where the exalted Jänakī is, remain uninjured by him.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.796,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040017","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"31255712e997f0bbb333d8283c1dda413268979b588c1ca0916dad09be9b0146","compact":"a63d6688858ee11f5d98cf3fc906a27f35853bb7e1dd89593e71017db5bd4b9e","nasal":"a63d6688858ee11f5d98cf3fc906a27f35853bb7e1dd89593e71017db5bd4b9e"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-18","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":18,"english":"Whether for preserving Jānakī, or from fatigue—it dose not appear. But what is his fatigue? She it is that has been preserved by him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040018","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"70692b94e59f87388227e0abe90c34c90670513f9f512ceb18df9ec862b15085","compact":"2eeaf67dc7ceb56ae484e77e5eedf15ed52034527aa4c58e932091b74be2d13b","nasal":"2eeaf67dc7ceb56ae484e77e5eedf15ed52034527aa4c58e932091b74be2d13b"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-19","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":19,"english":"And that overgrown Sinsapă tree, affluent with elegant foliage, under which Sītā herself has (always rested), has been spared by him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040019","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b2848fe382cdf5c5a6c42ab0c662ff70dfe579d2055f9bc020e2b21c8d8a865c","compact":"8b08a4032710932f8e6c48dfcb4b998778ca3e5f9364771cce2aa9769a714d2a","nasal":"8b08a4032710932f8e6c48dfcb4b998778ca3e5f9364771cce2aa9769a714d2a"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-20","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":20,"english":"It behove you to order sharp chastisement to be inflicted on that one of a fierce form, who, having carried on converse with Sītā, has laid your wood waste. Who, O Sovereign of the Rākşasas, that has not his life served from him, converse with Sītā, who has captivated your heart?\"","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.662,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040020","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c78001ffe9c549f5ec89139017999cd0ccf0025beec7bbd947e3c561b85f861a","compact":"103572bf1f185096284598d7c48305a11125f8d5de76f28e1ad7e360d9f26c5e","nasal":"b41bf8400d479a4c5c6b2c7d2289a455e8b209bdbc356483ce990a439514905c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-21","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":21,"english":"It behove you to order sharp chastisement to be inflicted on that one of a fierce form, who, having carried on converse with Sītā, has laid your wood waste. Who, O Sovereign of the Rākşasas, that has not his life served from him, converse with Sītā, who has captivated your heart?\"","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040021","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"60d930e537fd307b77785324affcbe5e92e136927e29c4d3bb639450c5585f2a","compact":"2c672f7b54bb4fdae92cabbc1ce2b3328a6fe5ac41aaafe7a2f20993f60c64aa","nasal":"2c672f7b54bb4fdae92cabbc1ce2b3328a6fe5ac41aaafe7a2f20993f60c64aa"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-22","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":22,"english":"Hearing the speeches of the Rākṣasīs, Rāvaņa, lord of Raksasas, with his eyes rolling in rage, flamed up like the fire of a funeral pyre.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.81,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040022","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"870561ed0d4b5d93bd2c5b9a8eeb7e1cafa119b38e09b04dba981c614c029644","compact":"1f55e3cbe49119526cffe154583ce5fec0c92000ea0d9f9ff34f36ec89d30ebb","nasal":"1f55e3cbe49119526cffe154583ce5fec0c92000ea0d9f9ff34f36ec89d30ebb"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-23","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":23,"english":"And that highly energetic one ordered his heroic servants, resembling himself, to punish Hanuman.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.646,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040023","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"08f8dc61599dd1dd002020ab530c6e2dbc54eb1f84b6ba6088b06d97c1393e5e","compact":"a8aac3b364779be0a609bdd090d0ad5c13e4dc722e95100859243fae3cc54666","nasal":"3bf9b079dc64eacf02017d5bb96fd9dc4e8177abe3f0c11b0fe0fad64293e064"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-24","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":24,"english":"And from that mansion speedily issued eighty thousand of those retainers, carrying in their hands maces and mallets. (Kūța-hammer. The commentator, however, says that it means a weapon resembling a hammer.)","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040024","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6ea8ca1ad42b488906a1ad8cd468f05d104db1d5d65d00bc8e967925d2119715","compact":"71274de3b1e29b466551bd564de6ba9f3e273d814c73a59318158a075b3b0120","nasal":"71274de3b1e29b466551bd564de6ba9f3e273d814c73a59318158a075b3b0120"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-25","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":25,"english":"Having huge bellies, and large teeth, of dreadful form, and possessed of unwieldy strength, all eager to engage in the conflict and take Hanuman.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040025","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b80ee2a78158cd51a5d1301bf55e7267896c7d51105bbfbbe8728bccf12e168b","compact":"b8ad0ed60b38fb2f8994cbce06953adc48025822ac796b4657cdc418c2a9e244","nasal":"b8ad0ed60b38fb2f8994cbce06953adc48025822ac796b4657cdc418c2a9e244"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-26","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":26,"english":"Having come near that monkey staying at the main entrance, those swelling spirits rushed on, even as insects rush into a flame.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.893,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040026","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8beffde481f9dc8ae0fe1420ad3573dddb2139d6a5995143d576acc71ed81558","compact":"1be3b9e50213d41c64237ba023e4f2493d99ed6de8bb840b3f056235399a1a94","nasal":"30c6de096efa8c957b0fe3f485b52294c6d7a6ef3eca8185d3e912ec0a5c2c56"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-27","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":40,"verse":27,"english":"And equipped with variegated maces, and bludgeons, and golden Angadas, (A bracelet worn on the upper arm) and arrows resembling the Sun, they approached that foremost of monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.739,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-42-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5040027","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fc3b7abf19485dc6c441582f5e40d26797b123603e72966d59e34fb83d2f497b","compact":"5178f220bde52c3853cb967b3a0cfd8feebdd08ff0425e9afb38659457665826","nasal":"34211741237fa8221329a36459633a32d71a4c128ed59f70b79e405a6f665004"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-40-28","kand